organizations, or events.)

7
00:00:30,240 --> 00:00:34,960
♪Birthday but with me♪

8
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,320
♪Every time, it's just me and me only♪

9
00:00:38,320 --> 00:00:41,960
♪What's this feeling? I've got no clue,♪

10
00:00:42,080 --> 00:00:44,000
♪Could it be I'm missing you?♪

11
00:00:44,040 --> 00:00:45,400
♪(Am I missing you?)♪

12
00:00:45,440 --> 00:00:50,200
♪Birthday but with me♪

13
00:00:50,240 --> 00:00:53,320
♪Why is it always happening to me?♪

14
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:57,080
♪The more it happens, the more I see♪

15
00:00:57,720 --> 00:00:59,960
♪Yeah, it must be♪

16
00:01:08,080 --> 00:01:10,280
(Waroros Market)

17
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:13,640
(B.S. Brothers On the Go)

18
00:01:13,680 --> 00:01:14,720
(Vlog with Laem)

19
00:01:14,760 --> 00:01:16,560
- We're at the market!
- This is Kad Laung.

20
00:01:16,600 --> 00:01:18,680
- Everything looks so good. Look!
- Look at these coconut rolls.

21
00:01:18,720 --> 00:01:19,400
(Wanna try some?)

22
00:01:20,760 --> 00:01:22,160
Everything looks delicious, right?

23
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:23,400
My mouth is watering. Look.

24
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:28,000
(Who's doing what?)

25
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:30,240
(Confused)

26
00:01:35,480 --> 00:01:36,800
- Oh, is this place famous?
- Here!

27
00:01:36,840 --> 00:01:37,800
That's a famous place.

28
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:42,520
(What should we get?)

29
00:01:43,160 --> 00:01:45,280
(Isn't this too close?)
Someone's hungry.

30
00:01:46,360 --> 00:01:47,720
Aren't you hungry, too?

31
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:49,400
I'm starving...

32
00:01:50,080 --> 00:01:51,200
just from following you around.

33
00:01:53,320 --> 00:01:54,760
I see.

34
00:01:55,520 --> 00:01:57,000
(Not over snacks yet)

35
00:01:57,960 --> 00:02:00,600
Hey, P'Three,
what are you standing around for?

36
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:04,400
(Aw!)

37
00:02:04,440 --> 00:02:05,440
Come with me.

38
00:02:05,480 --> 00:02:06,560
(Soh is away.
It's just Laem now.)

39
00:02:06,640 --> 00:02:09,120
- This one's handsome.
- You again?

40
00:02:10,080 --> 00:02:12,080
Before we head up the mountain,

41
00:02:12,120 --> 00:02:14,040
(Finally, a new cameraman)
I'm going to sacrifice my hair and...

42
00:02:14,080 --> 00:02:18,080
(So cute)
let the new hairstylist have a go at it.

43
00:02:18,160 --> 00:02:20,520
Let's see how my hair turns out

44
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:22,320
and how handsome I'll look
after the styling.

45
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:23,240
You'll definitely look good

46
00:02:23,280 --> 00:02:25,680
because I've watched
plenty of YouTube tutorials.

47
00:02:25,720 --> 00:02:28,160
(Styling or struggling?)
Trust me, you'll look stunning.

48
00:02:28,520 --> 00:02:29,680
Don't you worry.

49
00:02:29,680 --> 00:02:30,920
I wasn't worried at all.

50
00:02:30,920 --> 00:02:34,360
You know, with this face,
I can pull off any hairstyle.

51
00:02:35,680 --> 00:02:36,680
- Ready?
- Yeah.

52
00:02:36,720 --> 00:02:38,120
- Alright, let's do this.
- Let's go.

53
00:02:39,720 --> 00:02:40,720
- Starting now.
- Go for it.

54
00:02:40,760 --> 00:02:41,640
One, two, three.

55
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:51,000
Sh*t!

56
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:55,680
Are you for real?

57
00:02:56,200 --> 00:02:58,360
Well, you were facing away from me.

58
00:02:58,360 --> 00:03:00,200
How am I supposed to style it properly?

59
00:03:00,760 --> 00:03:03,800
Oh, I see.

60
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:05,400
Okay. Alright.

61
00:03:07,920 --> 00:03:09,080
P'Three, what are you doing?

62
00:03:09,120 --> 00:03:12,280
Well, didn't you say you couldn't do it
because I was facing away?

63
00:03:12,320 --> 00:03:13,720
Now I'm facing you.

64
00:03:15,280 --> 00:03:16,440
Smooth move, huh?

65
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:18,560
So, do I look handsome yet?

66
00:03:21,560 --> 00:03:22,960
I'm trying my best here.

67
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:24,000
I'll just...

68
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:27,160
let you check the mirror yourself.

69
00:03:27,520 --> 00:03:29,680
No, that's not what I meant.

70
00:03:29,720 --> 00:03:31,960
I was asking if you thought
I looked handsome in your eyes.

71
00:03:33,560 --> 00:03:36,600
Oh, look who's blushing! Gotcha!

72
00:03:36,600 --> 00:03:38,760
I know I'm just too irresistible.

73
00:03:40,200 --> 00:03:41,720
- Maybe not.
- Hey!

74
00:03:41,840 --> 00:03:43,360
I didn't say that.

75
00:03:44,280 --> 00:03:45,600
Don't just jump to conclusions.

76
00:03:45,640 --> 00:03:48,280
My, my, you're becoming
quite stubborn lately.

77
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:49,840
Where did you learn that from?

78
00:03:50,320 --> 00:03:52,720
- You're so adorable. Come here!
- Ow, P'Three!

79
00:03:52,760 --> 00:03:53,800
- P'Three!
- Come here.

80
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:54,760
- P'Three...
- Come on!

81
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:55,480
P'Three...

82
00:03:55,600 --> 00:03:57,600
The fans are going crazy.

83
00:03:57,640 --> 00:03:58,880
Three and Soh are being so lovey-dovey,

84
00:03:58,920 --> 00:04:03,120
leading hundreds of thousands of fans
to subscribe to BS BROTHERS.

85
00:04:03,240 --> 00:04:05,440
The team's popularity...

86
00:04:05,480 --> 00:04:08,400
skyrocketed,
finally overtaking Blue Viper.

87
00:04:08,440 --> 00:04:11,360
A major change is coming to Blue Viper.

88
00:04:11,360 --> 00:04:12,680
As they part ways with Ten,

89
00:04:12,720 --> 00:04:15,000
their long-time substitute player.

90
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:17,200
Word has it the split
wasn't on the best of terms.

91
00:04:17,640 --> 00:04:20,080
Oh, wait a second.
We have some breaking news.

92
00:04:20,400 --> 00:04:25,240
Breaking, PreawPreaw of B.S. Brothers
is facing a ban

93
00:04:25,400 --> 00:04:28,080
after allegedly violating the rules
with a mountain of evidence.

94
00:04:28,240 --> 00:04:30,800
Will B.S. Brothers be able
to move forward?

95
00:04:30,840 --> 00:04:31,720
(Suspension Announcement)

96
00:04:31,760 --> 00:04:36,200
"PreawPreaw has violated the rules
regarding elo boosting,"

97
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:38,520
"also known as paid rank boosting."

98
00:04:38,600 --> 00:04:40,800
"The ruling has been made
to penalize the player"

99
00:04:40,840 --> 00:04:42,680
"by suspending her
from all competitions"

100
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:44,960
"for two years."

101
00:04:45,440 --> 00:04:46,520
Sh*t.

102
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:48,640
Is this for real, Preaw?

103
00:04:51,280 --> 00:04:54,880
I didn't know. I was just a kid.

104
00:04:55,760 --> 00:04:58,160
I thought I could make some money
by playing games,

105
00:04:58,200 --> 00:05:00,080
so I did it.

106
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:03,120
But that was only one time.

107
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:07,560
It was so long ago. I was still a kid.

108
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:10,480
People somehow dug it back up.

109
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:13,240
Listen to me.

110
00:05:13,440 --> 00:05:15,360
Even if you only did it once,

111
00:05:15,680 --> 00:05:17,240
it's still a violation.

112
00:05:18,680 --> 00:05:20,800
You shouldn't have
thrown your future away like that.

113
00:05:21,880 --> 00:05:22,720
I'm sorry.

114
00:05:24,920 --> 00:05:26,160
Everyone, please calm down.

115
00:05:27,800 --> 00:05:30,640
Preaw is already upset enough as it is.

116
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:33,360
As for the mistakes that were made,

117
00:05:34,360 --> 00:05:36,760
we should focus
on finding a solution instead.

118
00:05:41,160 --> 00:05:43,400
Yeah, what's done is done. Let it go.

119
00:05:43,520 --> 00:05:46,520
The real question is...
who are we gonna get to replace her?

120
00:05:46,880 --> 00:05:47,880
Yeah, that's a good point.

121
00:05:48,760 --> 00:05:51,000
Where are we going to find
another Carry like her?

122
00:05:51,120 --> 00:05:54,120
All the talented players have likely
been snatched up by other teams.

123
00:05:54,240 --> 00:05:56,120
And we've got only a month left

124
00:05:56,600 --> 00:05:58,760
until the APL.

125
00:05:58,920 --> 00:06:00,560
To find a replacement for Preaw,

126
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:03,000
we need someone
whose playstyle matches yours,

127
00:06:03,160 --> 00:06:05,880
and other teams
shouldn't be poaching them.

128
00:06:06,080 --> 00:06:08,200
To put it simply, they've got to be...

129
00:06:08,520 --> 00:06:11,600
the rising star
waiting for their moment.

130
00:06:15,960 --> 00:06:16,840
- We're ready...
- We're ready...

131
00:06:16,920 --> 00:06:18,160
I have someone in mind.

132
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:19,920
Maybe not now.

133
00:06:21,240 --> 00:06:22,080
Who is it?

134
00:06:33,600 --> 00:06:35,240
- One on the rocks, please.
- You got it

135
00:06:48,920 --> 00:06:50,400
Since you got back from Chiang Mai,

136
00:06:50,920 --> 00:06:52,360
you've been nowhere to be found.

137
00:06:56,960 --> 00:06:58,000
How've you been?

138
00:07:02,120 --> 00:07:04,560
Being unemployed
has actually been quite a relief.

139
00:07:06,160 --> 00:07:08,800
Is there a reason
you asked me to meet you here?

140
00:07:12,720 --> 00:07:13,520
There is.

141
00:07:17,120 --> 00:07:17,840
Well...

142
00:07:20,160 --> 00:07:21,720
What would you think

143
00:07:22,280 --> 00:07:26,200
if I were to ask you...

144
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:38,040
to join B.S. Brothers?

145
00:07:43,240 --> 00:07:44,320
Are you insane?

146
00:07:45,160 --> 00:07:47,040
I just left Blue Viper.

147
00:07:48,120 --> 00:07:49,080
Besides,

148
00:07:49,880 --> 00:07:51,600
would your teammates even accept me?

149
00:07:52,880 --> 00:07:54,520
I'm running out of time here.

150
00:07:55,440 --> 00:07:58,720
We need someone with solid skills
who can gel with us,

151
00:07:59,680 --> 00:08:02,040
and I couldn't think of anyone but you.

152
00:08:05,040 --> 00:08:07,400
I won't argue with you about skills.

153
00:08:08,400 --> 00:08:10,880
But whether I'll fit in
with your team or not,

154
00:08:11,880 --> 00:08:12,920
I don't think I will.

155
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:23,160
But we've played together before,
haven't we?

156
00:08:24,320 --> 00:08:25,480
At the very least,

157
00:08:26,440 --> 00:08:27,680
you should know better than anyone

158
00:08:28,080 --> 00:08:29,680
how Three and I play.

159
00:08:34,440 --> 00:08:35,280
I'm sure

160
00:08:35,840 --> 00:08:38,480
that you can be the Carry
for B.S. Brothers.

161
00:08:49,600 --> 00:08:51,520
You won't have to be a substitute,

162
00:08:52,480 --> 00:08:53,760
waiting to sub in and out
for someone else.

163
00:08:57,880 --> 00:08:58,920
With me,

164
00:08:59,920 --> 00:09:01,080
you'll be in the starting lineup.

165
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:14,120
(We are B.S. Brothers)

166
00:09:16,920 --> 00:09:18,640
Are you seriously doing this, Preaw?

167
00:09:19,560 --> 00:09:20,840
Before I became a gamer,

168
00:09:21,200 --> 00:09:22,800
my aunt trained me in this.

169
00:09:23,680 --> 00:09:26,480
I never thought I'd have to use it
for our team today.

170
00:09:45,320 --> 00:09:48,160
Each of you, pick a card
and ask your question.

171
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:12,760
My question is...

172
00:10:12,920 --> 00:10:16,000
who is Jack bringing in
as a replacement?

173
00:10:16,400 --> 00:10:17,760
And will they be as good as you?

174
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:19,080
Will they get along with us?

175
00:10:19,280 --> 00:10:20,000
Pretty or not?

176
00:10:21,160 --> 00:10:22,320
Is now really the time?

177
00:10:22,720 --> 00:10:24,120
Wait, what?

178
00:10:24,120 --> 00:10:25,880
I was just asking.

179
00:10:25,920 --> 00:10:27,400
- I'm being serious here.
- Exactly.

180
00:10:29,040 --> 00:10:30,480
I know you wanna know it, too.

181
00:10:33,840 --> 00:10:34,800
The Tower.

182
00:10:35,160 --> 00:10:36,960
You might receive news
you're not prepared for.

183
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:42,200
- Death?
- We're gonna die?

184
00:10:42,800 --> 00:10:43,840
No.

185
00:10:44,360 --> 00:10:46,120
Bad things will gradually
turn into good ones.

186
00:10:46,440 --> 00:10:47,560
That's good to hear.

187
00:10:49,600 --> 00:10:50,320
The Sun...

188
00:10:50,360 --> 00:10:53,480
Light, growth, and vitality.

189
00:11:00,400 --> 00:11:01,440
The person who's coming...

190
00:11:02,200 --> 00:11:04,000
will be a knight in shining armor.

191
00:11:04,360 --> 00:11:05,800
They're coming to help us.

192
00:11:06,760 --> 00:11:07,760
I'm calling it.

193
00:11:08,760 --> 00:11:10,480
Are you making this up
based on the cards?

194
00:11:10,720 --> 00:11:13,440
- A knight in shining armor...
- You're making it up, aren't you?

195
00:11:15,840 --> 00:11:16,600
Guys,

196
00:11:17,680 --> 00:11:20,160
I've gotten our new Carry.

197
00:11:30,120 --> 00:11:33,080
Your knight in shining armor is here.

198
00:11:38,520 --> 00:11:40,400
You can't get away from me, Three.

199
00:11:42,240 --> 00:11:43,960
Come on, let's go.

200
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:45,400
Listen to what the others have to say.

201
00:11:46,160 --> 00:11:47,240
Look at that stare.

202
00:11:47,640 --> 00:11:49,360
Are you planning on staring all day?

203
00:11:49,360 --> 00:11:50,320
Go sit down.

204
00:11:50,800 --> 00:11:51,720
Listen to what we have to say.

205
00:11:51,720 --> 00:11:53,160
Wait, where are you going?

206
00:11:53,240 --> 00:11:54,400
Sit down.

207
00:11:55,240 --> 00:11:56,400
Jeez.

208
00:12:01,440 --> 00:12:02,160
Won't say anything?

209
00:12:03,640 --> 00:12:04,720
Should we...

210
00:12:04,880 --> 00:12:05,560
Listen.

211
00:12:08,280 --> 00:12:09,120
P'Jack,

212
00:12:09,480 --> 00:12:11,680
why are you bringing a traitor
into our midst?

213
00:12:12,520 --> 00:12:13,840
Would you guys just listen to me?

214
00:12:13,840 --> 00:12:15,560
What the f*ck do you have to say?

215
00:12:15,560 --> 00:12:16,840
What the hell were you thinking?

216
00:12:17,160 --> 00:12:18,720
You know he can't be trusted.

217
00:12:19,200 --> 00:12:20,000
Wait a minute.

218
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:20,720
When we were in Chiang Mai,

219
00:12:20,720 --> 00:12:23,000
you already talked to him nicely,
didn't you?

220
00:12:23,080 --> 00:12:24,160
I only agreed to talk to him.

221
00:12:24,200 --> 00:12:25,880
I didn't trust him enough
to let him join our team.

222
00:12:26,680 --> 00:12:29,160
Who knows if he's scheming
with Blue Viper.

223
00:12:33,240 --> 00:12:35,440
As for that, you guys can rest easy.

224
00:12:35,800 --> 00:12:37,360
Ten hasn't been in contact
with Blue Viper

225
00:12:37,360 --> 00:12:38,960
since we got back from Chiang Mai.

226
00:12:39,920 --> 00:12:42,120
I know that to you guys,

227
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:45,040
he might not seem all that trustworthy.

228
00:12:45,960 --> 00:12:47,440
But with the time we have left,

229
00:12:48,040 --> 00:12:50,800
I don't trust
anyone else's skills but his.

230
00:12:52,680 --> 00:12:54,120
People make mistakes.

231
00:12:56,720 --> 00:12:57,840
But I believe...

232
00:12:59,120 --> 00:13:00,800
that if they're given a second chance,

233
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:03,080
nobody wants to repeat
the same mistakes.

234
00:13:06,640 --> 00:13:08,520
I'm with Jack and Soh on this.

235
00:13:09,560 --> 00:13:11,080
Just chill out, man.

236
00:13:11,080 --> 00:13:12,440
Think about it carefully.

237
00:13:13,200 --> 00:13:14,600
But if you really don't trust him,

238
00:13:14,880 --> 00:13:17,720
you can have Laem keep an eye on him.

239
00:13:17,960 --> 00:13:18,960
He's like a loyal watchdog.

240
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:21,000
That way, Ten won't be able
to pull anything on you.

241
00:13:21,600 --> 00:13:22,360
Right, boy?

242
00:13:23,840 --> 00:13:25,080
I can't catch a break.

243
00:13:25,080 --> 00:13:26,520
Are you low-key calling me a dog?

244
00:13:29,200 --> 00:13:29,920
Tell you what.

245
00:13:30,800 --> 00:13:32,040
Let P'Pech make the call

246
00:13:32,600 --> 00:13:34,160
since he's been with us since day one.

247
00:13:34,280 --> 00:13:36,000
He knows exactly
what kind of jerk this guy is.

248
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:39,640
And if P'Pech insists
on letting him join the team,

249
00:13:40,080 --> 00:13:41,160
then I'll give up.

250
00:13:42,440 --> 00:13:45,400
But I'm sure P'Pech will see it my way.

251
00:13:46,320 --> 00:13:48,880
Welcome to B.S. Brothers, Ten.

252
00:13:49,280 --> 00:13:51,680
I thought that after Preaw got banned,

253
00:13:51,720 --> 00:13:54,120
the team would be in total shambles.

254
00:13:54,560 --> 00:13:56,520
It's a good thing
Ten came to the rescue.

255
00:13:58,040 --> 00:13:59,680
It's what I have to do anyway.

256
00:13:59,800 --> 00:14:00,480
F*ck that.

257
00:14:00,800 --> 00:14:02,600
You got kicked out by your old team.

258
00:14:02,720 --> 00:14:03,520
P'Three,

259
00:14:04,400 --> 00:14:05,560
that's not very nice.

260
00:14:06,440 --> 00:14:07,200
Okay.

261
00:14:08,720 --> 00:14:10,080
Aw!

262
00:14:10,400 --> 00:14:12,680
Looks like even P'Three
is scared of his boyfriend, too.

263
00:14:13,160 --> 00:14:14,240
I'm not scared.

264
00:14:17,080 --> 00:14:18,600
I just respect him.

265
00:14:19,080 --> 00:14:19,880
Oh, I see.

266
