CEO of a top computer hardware company.

794
00:44:19,240 --> 00:44:21,640
He was caught red-handed

795
00:44:21,680 --> 00:44:24,960
taking a mystery woman
who wasn't his wife to a concert.

796
00:44:25,240 --> 00:44:28,160
His wife released a tearful video

797
00:44:28,160 --> 00:44:30,040
exposing him for all to see.

798
00:44:30,040 --> 00:44:32,160
But the scandal doesn't stop there.

799
00:44:32,160 --> 00:44:33,520
Netizens have dug up...

800
00:44:33,560 --> 00:44:36,800
PECHTECH's financial records

801
00:44:36,960 --> 00:44:39,240
(Balance Sheet of PECHTECH Co., Ltd.)
and even looked into

802
00:44:39,240 --> 00:44:40,680
its esports team, B.S. Brothers.

803
00:44:40,680 --> 00:44:45,000
It was discovered the players
have been owed salaries for years,

804
00:44:45,000 --> 00:44:46,920
totaling nearly a million baht.

805
00:44:46,960 --> 00:44:50,880
He only started paying on time
after the team became RPL runners-up.

806
00:44:50,880 --> 00:44:51,800
Honestly,

807
00:44:51,840 --> 00:44:54,760
this is a serious violation
of the league's rules.

808
00:44:58,120 --> 00:44:59,560
P'Pech, seriously?

809
00:44:59,720 --> 00:45:02,040
Why did you have to mess around
at a time like this?

810
00:45:03,840 --> 00:45:05,400
We're officially screwed.

811
00:45:06,520 --> 00:45:08,640
P'Pech's secretary called me

812
00:45:09,080 --> 00:45:10,440
and said that our team...

813
00:45:10,440 --> 00:45:12,440
is at risk of being disqualified
from the tournament.

814
00:45:12,640 --> 00:45:13,600
- What?
- What?

815
00:45:15,920 --> 00:45:19,800
P'Pech's reputation in the league
is in the gutter right now.

816
00:45:20,120 --> 00:45:22,880
The league management said

817
00:45:23,040 --> 00:45:25,760
our team needs to
settle the debt immediately,

818
00:45:26,000 --> 00:45:29,920
and we need a financial guarantee
for the players' salaries.

819
00:45:30,680 --> 00:45:31,960
What the hell?

820
00:45:32,080 --> 00:45:32,920
Sh*t.

821
00:45:33,600 --> 00:45:35,360
Are we cursed this year or something?

822
00:45:38,000 --> 00:45:40,160
Is the financial guarantee
the only option?

823
00:45:40,320 --> 00:45:41,520
Isn't there any other way?

824
00:45:42,240 --> 00:45:43,800
Where's P'Pech, though?

825
00:45:44,640 --> 00:45:46,280
That bastard turned off his phone.

826
00:45:46,560 --> 00:45:48,600
That's why
his secretary called me instead.

827
00:45:50,480 --> 00:45:51,480
This is insane.

828
00:45:51,680 --> 00:45:53,960
The owner's problems
have nothing to do with us!

829
00:45:56,200 --> 00:45:58,360
- I'm losing it.
- This is bullsh*t.

830
00:46:00,480 --> 00:46:01,760
Making a fuss won't change anything.

831
00:46:02,200 --> 00:46:04,720
We need to come up with the money

832
00:46:05,200 --> 00:46:06,640
or get ourselves a new team owner.

833
00:46:07,240 --> 00:46:08,040
Hey.

834
00:46:08,400 --> 00:46:10,960
The APL starts in less than a week.

835
00:46:11,000 --> 00:46:12,320
How are we supposed to find a new owner?

836
00:46:12,360 --> 00:46:13,640
We have to try, don't we?

837
00:46:20,600 --> 00:46:23,040
Ten, Jack, you two come with me.

838
00:46:23,280 --> 00:46:24,800
Let's talk to our old sponsors

839
00:46:24,840 --> 00:46:26,200
and hit up
whatever connections we've got

840
00:46:26,800 --> 00:46:28,400
to ask if they're interested
in taking over our team.

841
00:46:29,320 --> 00:46:31,840
P'Toobtub, Laem, Soh.

842
00:46:32,120 --> 00:46:34,080
Help me out
by calling the major sponsors.

843
00:46:34,080 --> 00:46:36,000
Also, stay on standby

844
00:46:36,200 --> 00:46:38,520
in case the league reaches out
with anything urgent.

845
00:46:39,360 --> 00:46:40,280
Got it.

846
00:46:40,520 --> 00:46:41,840
I'll handle things on this end.

847
00:46:42,240 --> 00:46:43,320
Let's go, guys.

848
00:46:43,960 --> 00:46:45,040
- Let's go.
- Right behind you.

849
00:46:46,040 --> 00:46:48,440
I think I have their contacts.
Let me pull them up.

850
00:47:10,880 --> 00:47:12,000
What are you doing?

851
00:47:15,480 --> 00:47:16,560
I'm beat.

852
00:47:20,080 --> 00:47:21,400
Totally exhausted.

853
00:47:35,200 --> 00:47:36,560
How's it going?

854
00:47:43,320 --> 00:47:44,960
The timing is just too tight.

855
00:47:45,480 --> 00:47:48,600
And many companies have already
closed out their budgets.

856
00:47:51,320 --> 00:47:55,560
Getting a massive sum of money
at such short notice is tough.

857
00:47:56,960 --> 00:47:57,800
That's true.

858
00:47:59,120 --> 00:48:00,840
I've also called quite a few places,

859
00:48:01,080 --> 00:48:02,840
but none of them have gotten back to me.

860
00:48:11,360 --> 00:48:12,560
It's okay.

861
00:48:14,040 --> 00:48:16,080
We'll try again tomorrow, alright?

862
00:48:18,200 --> 00:48:20,120
We'll find a way out of this.

863
00:48:24,640 --> 00:48:26,280
What's that smell? Smells so good.

864
00:48:28,040 --> 00:48:30,720
Is Chef Soh on duty today?

865
00:48:30,760 --> 00:48:33,000
Whoa, what's for dinner?

866
00:48:33,600 --> 00:48:34,640
Look at that.

867
00:48:36,800 --> 00:48:38,120
Everything looks delicious.

868
00:48:45,280 --> 00:48:46,040
Hello?

869
00:48:46,920 --> 00:48:48,000
This is Soh speaking.

870
00:48:48,280 --> 00:48:50,120
Who is this?

871
00:48:56,560 --> 00:48:57,400
Been waiting long?

872
00:49:01,000 --> 00:49:02,040
Not at all.

873
00:49:03,760 --> 00:49:04,360
Okay.

874
00:49:04,760 --> 00:49:05,680
Let's get down to business.

875
00:49:06,560 --> 00:49:08,160
Actually, my team manager

876
00:49:08,720 --> 00:49:12,760
can help your team
get to the APL in time.

877
00:49:13,440 --> 00:49:14,240
Really?

878
00:49:15,200 --> 00:49:16,000
Yeah.

879
00:49:19,920 --> 00:49:20,880
But...

880
00:49:21,920 --> 00:49:23,680
there's a catch.

881
00:49:37,320 --> 00:49:39,440
Why are you guys looking so serious?

882
00:49:54,600 --> 00:49:55,400
Peem?

883
00:49:56,880 --> 00:49:58,280
What's his business with Soh?

884
00:49:59,960 --> 00:50:01,760
People are trashing Soh
all over the internet.

885
00:50:02,800 --> 00:50:04,720
They're saying
our team is falling apart.

886
00:50:05,520 --> 00:50:09,040
I can't blame him
for looking for a way out.

887
00:50:09,960 --> 00:50:12,960
Everyone's calling him a traitor,

888
00:50:13,640 --> 00:50:15,000
saying he betrayed us.

889
00:50:29,000 --> 00:50:30,800
Why are you sitting here
all alone in the dark?

890
00:50:32,440 --> 00:50:33,920
What are you planning to do?

891
00:50:40,720 --> 00:50:42,160
What did Peem say to you?

892
00:50:47,600 --> 00:50:48,920
Blue Viper...

893
00:50:51,000 --> 00:50:52,920
is going to settle our salaries for us.

894
00:50:53,320 --> 00:50:55,040
And what's the price for that?

895
00:50:56,920 --> 00:50:58,000
Are you the price?

896
00:50:59,880 --> 00:51:00,440
Yes.

897
00:51:00,920 --> 00:51:03,280
Next season, I have to join them.

898
00:51:04,880 --> 00:51:05,920
I'm not letting you go.

899
00:51:06,120 --> 00:51:07,560
We're on the same team, Soh.

900
00:51:10,800 --> 00:51:13,040
If there's a problem,
we have to solve it together.

901
00:51:13,720 --> 00:51:16,320
There's no reason
for you to sacrifice yourself like this.

902
00:51:16,320 --> 00:51:17,960
It's because we are on the same team.

903
00:51:20,600 --> 00:51:22,720
I don't want to see our team
in this situation.

904
00:51:24,880 --> 00:51:28,320
Besides, B.S. Brothers has come so far.

905
00:51:29,080 --> 00:51:30,920
Since we have this chance,

906
00:51:31,000 --> 00:51:32,440
shouldn't we take it?

907
00:51:32,920 --> 00:51:34,400
But what's the trade-off?

908
00:51:36,640 --> 00:51:40,120
The fact that we won't have you
on our team next year?

909
00:51:45,320 --> 00:51:48,360
This is probably the best way, P'Three.

910
00:51:49,600 --> 00:51:51,320
We have no other choice.

911
00:51:54,240 --> 00:51:55,400
Who says we don't?

912
00:52:03,960 --> 00:52:05,560
How am I supposed
to come up with the money?

913
00:52:14,120 --> 00:52:15,840
F*ck it.
There goes my electricity bill.

914
00:52:16,640 --> 00:52:17,960
Let's use it for now.

915
00:52:21,040 --> 00:52:22,760
Come on over!

916
00:52:22,880 --> 00:52:25,320
Step right up, everyone!

917
00:52:25,400 --> 00:52:27,080
B.S. Brothers shirts are now on sale!

918
00:52:27,120 --> 00:52:29,800
They're limited edition, one-of-a-kind.

919
00:52:29,840 --> 00:52:31,000
Every piece is unique

920
00:52:31,040 --> 00:52:34,360
because I have no damn clue
where the screen-printing screen went.

921
00:52:34,440 --> 00:52:35,480
Everyone,

922
00:52:35,520 --> 00:52:37,880
come buy everything at our stall!

923
00:52:37,880 --> 00:52:38,760
Hurry, hurry!

924
00:52:38,760 --> 00:52:41,560
- Come on over!
- They're limited edition!

925
00:52:41,640 --> 00:52:43,840
- Come on, you can take photos.
- Ten, Jack, you're so handsome!

926
00:52:43,840 --> 00:52:45,600
- Can we get a photo?
- Sure.

927
00:52:48,000 --> 00:52:49,240
You can take photos, everyone.

928
00:52:49,280 --> 00:52:50,240
Yeah, it's fine.

929
00:52:50,320 --> 00:52:51,720
But could you
support B.S. Brothers, too?

930
00:52:51,760 --> 00:52:53,200
- Alright, here.
- Here, this one.

931
00:52:53,240 --> 00:52:55,440
This lightstick is only 450.

932
00:52:55,640 --> 00:52:58,360
And this shirt
our handsome P'Ten is holding...

933
00:52:58,480 --> 00:53:00,480
is 500 baht. Pick whichever you want!

934
00:53:00,480 --> 00:53:01,760
- This one's a great deal.
- You can pick anything.

935
00:53:01,800 --> 00:53:03,560
Whoa, that's expensive.
Can you give us a discount?

936
00:53:03,560 --> 00:53:05,320
- Too expensive?
- It's quality.

937
00:53:05,320 --> 00:53:06,080
- Can you lower the price?
- Yes.

938
00:53:06,120 --> 00:53:07,360
Please give us a discount.

939
00:53:07,520 --> 00:53:08,760
Over here!

940
00:53:08,760 --> 00:53:11,520
Only a hundred!
Everything's just a hundred baht.

941
00:53:11,520 --> 00:53:13,280
Come on!

942
00:53:13,320 --> 00:53:15,760
Come take a look.
You can pick what you like.

943
00:53:15,920 --> 00:53:17,800
- Knockoffs come out fast these days.
- Everything's 100!

944
00:53:18,200 --> 00:53:20,160
- Go ahead, pick one.
- This isn't good.

945
00:53:20,280 --> 00:53:22,040
- Only a hundred.
- Hey, 99 baht over here!

946
00:53:22,040 --> 00:53:22,760
Only 99 baht!

947
00:53:22,800 --> 00:53:23,960
- Come on!
- Come on.

948
00:53:23,960 --> 00:53:25,840
- Only 99, take your pick.
- This one's nice.

949
00:53:25,840 --> 00:53:27,880
- 99 baht, hurry!
- This one is handsome.

950
00:53:27,920 --> 00:53:28,600
Good.

951
00:53:28,600 --> 00:53:30,520
50 baht!

952
00:53:30,560 --> 00:53:32,080
- Fifty?
- Fifty?

953
00:53:32,080 --> 00:53:33,000
Fif...

954
00:53:33,000 --> 00:53:33,960
50 baht?

955
00:53:33,960 --> 00:53:36,520
- Take your pick, guys!
- Let me calculate the costs...

956
00:53:37,320 --> 00:53:39,080
49 over here!

957
00:53:39,120 --> 00:53:40,200
- 49!
- 49?

958
00:53:40,520 --> 00:53:42,680
Come on, 49 baht!

959
00:53:48,360 --> 00:53:51,320
One thousand nine hundred and twenty,
plus some random change.

960
00:53:54,000 --> 00:53:54,840
I told you.

961
00:53:55,080 --> 00:53:56,320
Don't start a price war.

962
00:53:56,360 --> 00:53:58,720
Our cash flow is tight.
We're gonna go broke at this rate.

963
00:54:01,400 --> 00:54:02,720
Did you learn that from a series?

964
00:54:04,000 --> 00:54:06,600
Oh, come on. You can't play like that.

965
00:54:06,640 --> 00:54:07,960
Here, let me carry you.

966
00:54:08,000 --> 00:54:10,120
Come on, I'll carry you myself.

967
00:54:10,720 --> 00:54:12,280
Oh, look at that. That hurts.

968
00:54:12,320 --> 00:54:15,080
How's that? You're all crooked now.

969
00:54:15,120 --> 00:54:16,640
Ow...

970
00:54:17,160 --> 00:54:18,960
That's a total eyesore,

971
00:54:19,120 --> 00:54:20,000
but look at this.

972
00:54:20,840 --> 00:54:22,440
If you don't have
these blue-light glasses,

973
00:54:22,440 --> 00:54:23,560
you won't be able to
take your eyes off me.

974
00:54:25,280 --> 00:54:26,760
Do you know why?

975
00:54:26,800 --> 00:54:27,680
I don't want to brag,

976
00:54:27,720 --> 00:54:31,000
but look at this. These lenses
are made with space-age technology.

977
00:54:31,040 --> 00:54:32,200
Look at these frames.

978
00:54:33,000 --> 00:54:34,800
They're Vibranium.

979
00:54:35,040 --> 00:54:37,000
You don't believe me?

980
00:54:37,040 --> 00:54:39,800
You don't believe it?

981
00:54:39,840 --> 00:54:40,560
You...

982
00:54:41,560 --> 00:54:43,440
You don't believe me, do you?

983
00:54:45,520 --> 00:54:48,560
See? You don't believe me?

984
00:54:50,320 --> 00:54:51,400
Look at that!

985
00:54:51,440 --> 00:54:53,440
Told you they're tough,
drop-proof, and unbreakable.

986
00:54:56,160 --> 00:54:57,160
I'm not trying to flex.

987
00:54:58,480 --> 00:54:59,120
Come on.

988
00:55:00,200 --> 00:55:03,000
Are cooking games
this high-def these days?

989
00:55:03,040 --> 00:55:04,080
Whoa, crystal clear.

990
00:55:04,160 --> 00:55:05,880
This looks great. It's making me hungry.

991
00:55:05,920 --> 00:55:08,600
Hungry? Let's grab a grain bar.

992
00:55:09,600 --> 00:55:10,480
Here.

993
00:55:14,600 --> 00:55:17,240
It's heavenly, guys.

994
00:55:21,400 --> 00:55:24,160
(What's gotten into you?
Get some rest.)

995
00:55:24,640 --> 00:55:26,600
(This feels like an ad now. I'm out.)

996
00:55:28,880 --> 00:55:30,320
(Unfollowing you. This is too much.)

997
00:55:30,440 --> 00:55:34,120
Hey, wait a sec. Don't go yet!

998
00:55:35,080 --> 00:55:37,240
Why would you leave right now?

999
00:55:39,240 --> 00:55:40,400
How are you guys doing?

1000
00:55:40,840 --> 00:55:42,120
(Look, I'm telling you...)

1001
00:55:42,560 --> 00:55:45,240
If you guys keep selling stuff
at this market

1002
00:55:45,280 --> 00:55:47,040
for a whole year,
you still won't hit a million.

1003
00:55:49,120 --> 00:55:50,840
You guys have to face the truth.

1004
00:55:51,400 --> 00:55:53,160
We really have a money problem.

1005
00:55:54,160 --> 00:55:57,000
As for Soh,
he's just looking out for his friends.

1006
00:55:57,760 --> 00:56:00,760
Hey, we're B.S. Brothers.

1007
00:56:01,080 --> 00:56:03,040
Are we gonna give up this easily?

1008
00:56:03,880 --> 00:56:05,000
I think...

1009
00:56:05,360 --> 00:56:07,840
we should spend
our remaining time practicing.

1010
00:56:08,680 --> 00:56:10,680
We still have Soh for this tournament.

1011
00:56:10,920 --> 00:56:13,680
As for the next one, we'll cross
that bridge when we get to it.

1012
00:56:14,040 --> 00:56:15,040
P'Toobtub's right.

1013
00:56:15,600 --> 00:56:19,040
After the APL,
we're gonna be totally lost, though.

1014
00:56:19,440 --> 00:56:23,400
We'll have to find a replacement for Soh
next season anyway.

1015
00:56:26,080 --> 00:56:27,520
It's not your time yet.

1016
00:56:28,600 --> 00:56:30,800
Man, then when?

1017
00:56:33,680 --> 00:56:35,080
And what about you, Three?

1018
00:56:36,400 --> 00:56:37,240
What's your move?

1019
00:56:55,400 --> 00:56:58,480
(You should be able to give me
your answer tonight, right?)

1020
00:57:21,320 --> 00:57:22,560
(I've made my decision.)

1021
00:57:24,040 --> 00:57:26,120
(I'll choose the best path for you)

1022
00:57:26,400 --> 00:57:27,400
(and for our team.)

1023
00:57:28,000 --> 00:57:29,480
(See you at the APL.)

1024
00:57:35,280 --> 00:57:37,360
In the final stretch
before the transfer window closes,

1025
00:57:37,360 --> 00:57:39,120
rumors are swirling that

1026
00:57:39,200 --> 00:57:43,800
Blue Viper is set to snatch up
legendary player Derya for their roster.

1027
00:57:43,960 --> 00:57:45,240
Inside sources report that

1028
00:57:45,280 --> 00:57:50,120
they are ready to unveil Derya
at the Blue Viper fan meeting today.

1029
00:57:51,240 --> 00:57:53,080
Welcome to Blue Viper, bro.

1030
00:57:53,920 --> 00:57:55,040
See you next season.

1031
00:58:00,880 --> 00:58:03,280
Okay, Soh. Now put the jacket on.

1032
00:58:03,560 --> 00:58:04,880
We'll go sign the contract.

1033
00:58:08,480 --> 00:58:09,320
Welcome.

1034
00:58:10,880 --> 00:58:11,920
Congratulations.

1035
00:58:22,520 --> 00:58:24,800
Ladies and gentlemen, the wait is over.

1036
00:58:24,840 --> 00:58:26,440
It's time to introduce the newest member

1037
00:58:26,480 --> 00:58:28,760
joining the Unbeatable Kings.

1038
00:58:28,880 --> 00:58:33,960
Let's have a big round of applause
for Blue Viper's new member!

1039
00:58:50,200 --> 00:58:53,280
Alright, now that
the introductions are over,

1040
00:58:53,320 --> 00:58:54,240
next up,

1041
00:58:54,240 --> 00:58:57,680
I'd like to ask Derya
to sign the contract right now.

1042
00:59:14,760 --> 00:59:17,280
(Signature)

1043
00:59:17,880 --> 00:59:19,760
Soh, stop!

1044
00:59:22,280 --> 00:59:23,040
P'Three?

1045
00:59:25,240 --> 00:59:25,960
Soh!

1046
00:59:27,080 --> 00:59:29,560
Didn't I tell you
that I can't live without you?

1047
00:59:32,320 --> 00:59:33,560
It's not just Three.

1048
00:59:36,080 --> 00:59:37,200
It's all of us.

1049
00:59:38,840 --> 00:59:39,640
That's right.

1050
00:59:43,360 --> 00:59:45,040
You can't just barge in here like this.

1051
00:59:45,480 --> 00:59:46,680
Security!

1052
00:59:48,360 --> 00:59:50,160
Over my dead body!

1053
00:59:52,240 --> 00:59:53,080
They're strong as hell.

1054
00:59:53,200 --> 00:59:54,080
Go for it, buddy!

1055
00:59:57,360 --> 00:59:58,960
Are you sure
this is what you want to do?

1056
00:59:59,440 --> 01:00:02,200
Your team is about to be disqualified
from the league.

1057
01:00:02,280 --> 01:00:03,920
Don't you want to compete
in the APL anymore?

1058
01:00:13,520 --> 01:00:14,800
Did you really think

1059
01:00:15,240 --> 01:00:17,080
I'd show up here without a backup plan?

1060
01:00:43,880 --> 01:00:46,160
I can understand
your interest in the competition,

1061
01:00:46,880 --> 01:00:50,400
but risking this much money
without any guarantee,

1062
01:00:51,440 --> 01:00:52,880
it just doesn't sound worth it.

1063
01:01:00,320 --> 01:01:01,480
I know, Dad.

1064
01:01:02,120 --> 01:01:03,280
But this money...

1065
01:01:04,080 --> 01:01:05,440
isn't just for me.

1066
01:01:07,000 --> 01:01:08,640
It's for everyone
who has fought alongside me.

1067
01:01:09,960 --> 01:01:12,240
Soh was even willing
to sacrifice his own future.

1068
01:01:13,280 --> 01:01:15,640
If I let him face this all alone,

1069
01:01:16,480 --> 01:01:18,160
I wouldn't deserve
to be the team captain anymore.

1070
01:01:20,560 --> 01:01:21,360
Dad,

1071
01:01:23,080 --> 01:01:24,920
I know his reputation is in the gutter.

1072
01:01:25,240 --> 01:01:26,440
He's stubborn.

1073
01:01:26,720 --> 01:01:27,960
He runs away from his problems.

1074
01:01:28,920 --> 01:01:32,480
He even left the family business
for me to handle all by myself,

1075
01:01:32,480 --> 01:01:33,960
and he just ran off to play games.

1076
01:01:36,960 --> 01:01:38,400
Are you actually trying to help me?

1077
01:01:41,400 --> 01:01:42,640
But you see it, too,

1078
01:01:43,440 --> 01:01:46,000
that the only thing
he's never given up on

1079
01:01:46,200 --> 01:01:47,200
is gaming.

1080
01:01:49,680 --> 01:01:50,800
And all this time,

1081
01:01:51,360 --> 01:01:53,760
no matter how much
of a screw-up he's been,

1082
01:01:54,800 --> 01:01:57,560
he's never once begged you for anything.

1083
01:01:59,760 --> 01:02:00,600
He's headstrong

1084
01:02:01,080 --> 01:02:02,080
with a big ego.

1085
01:02:03,920 --> 01:02:07,120
But today, a guy like him
is willing to swallow his pride.

1086
01:02:07,880 --> 01:02:10,080
He's begging for your help

1087
01:02:11,080 --> 01:02:13,560
even though this is the place
he hates the most,

1088
01:02:14,040 --> 01:02:15,280
yet he's doing it anyway

1089
01:02:16,320 --> 01:02:17,800
just so his team can keep going.

1090
01:02:26,560 --> 01:02:27,400
Dad...

1091
01:02:29,560 --> 01:02:32,920
Can you please trust my loser brother
just this once?

1092
01:03:07,160 --> 01:03:10,400
If your team needs a new owner,

1093
01:03:11,320 --> 01:03:13,160
it should be under our family name.

1094
01:03:17,600 --> 01:03:19,320
But I have one condition.

1095
01:03:21,480 --> 01:03:23,840
You have to bring
that championship home.

1096
01:03:24,760 --> 01:03:25,560
Understand?

1097
01:03:28,320 --> 01:03:30,760
Yes, Dad. I promise.

1098
01:03:35,440 --> 01:03:37,520
Mom, don't just stand there smiling.

1099
01:03:38,200 --> 01:03:40,120
Come here, Mrs. Wanphen.

1100
01:03:43,600 --> 01:03:44,720
It's okay.

1101
01:03:44,760 --> 01:03:45,800
See? He said yes.

1102
01:03:45,840 --> 01:03:46,840
I told you so.

1103
01:03:48,760 --> 01:03:52,600
(B.S. Brothers by Saenganan)

1104
01:03:52,640 --> 01:03:54,360
I'd like to introduce everyone to...

1105
01:03:54,640 --> 01:03:58,360
the new sponsor
and owner of B.S. Brothers,

1106
01:03:58,960 --> 01:04:00,720
Saenganan Gold Shop.

1107
01:04:00,720 --> 01:04:03,680
(B.S. Brothers by Saenganan)

1108
01:04:07,200 --> 01:04:09,480
Whoa.

1109
01:04:10,040 --> 01:04:14,640
You sure we're still an esports team,
not some kind of walking billboards?

1110
01:04:15,120 --> 01:04:16,080
Shut up, Laem.

1111
01:04:16,400 --> 01:04:18,880
We're lucky enough
just to have a new owner.

1112
01:04:22,800 --> 01:04:23,920
My apologies,

1113
01:04:24,760 --> 01:04:27,280
but you can't take our player anywhere

1114
01:04:28,400 --> 01:04:31,240
because Soh already signed the contract.

1115
01:04:31,680 --> 01:04:35,120
The contract is now legally binding.

1116
01:04:42,360 --> 01:04:43,360
Maybe not yet.

1117
01:04:46,680 --> 01:04:49,160
I actually hadn't finished signing it.

1118
01:04:49,600 --> 01:04:51,240
P'Three interrupted me.

1119
01:04:53,240 --> 01:04:54,840
It's still missing an H.

1120
01:04:56,960 --> 01:04:58,000
Sh*t...

1121
01:04:58,600 --> 01:05:00,200
Soh is a total savage.

1122
01:05:00,920 --> 01:05:04,800
Whoa, so Wimp Viper signed with P'So,

1123
01:05:04,920 --> 01:05:07,360
- instead of Soh.
- It's P'So now.

1124
01:05:09,480 --> 01:05:10,560
What the heck?

1125
01:05:11,920 --> 01:05:13,480
What a total waste of my damn time.

1126
01:05:15,600 --> 01:05:16,680
To hell with it.

1127
01:05:16,840 --> 01:05:19,120
We'll win even without Soh.

1128
01:05:20,720 --> 01:05:21,480
Let's go.

1129
01:05:22,040 --> 01:05:23,840
If that's what you think,
then good for you.

1130
01:05:24,400 --> 01:05:26,480
See you at the APL.

1131
01:05:28,400 --> 01:05:29,040
Bring it.

1132
01:05:42,280 --> 01:05:43,480
You derpy kid.

1133
01:05:51,480 --> 01:05:52,720
(Another shocking twist in the scene!)

1134
01:05:52,720 --> 01:05:56,840
(Soh has suddenly announced
his departure from Blue Viper)

1135
01:05:57,000 --> 01:06:00,200
(after rumors of him joining the team
lasted less than five minutes.)

1136
01:06:00,400 --> 01:06:03,560
(He signed the contract,
only to tear it up moments later.)

1137
01:06:04,320 --> 01:06:06,560
And this incident has set the stage

1138
01:06:06,600 --> 01:06:09,440
for the upcoming match in the APL

1139
01:06:09,480 --> 01:06:11,880
between the defending champs,
Blue Viper,

1140
01:06:11,920 --> 01:06:14,040
and the dark horse, B.S. Brothers.

1141
01:06:14,080 --> 01:06:16,440
I'm telling you,
it's going to be intense.

1142
01:06:17,400 --> 01:06:18,240
P'Three...

1143
01:06:20,600 --> 01:06:22,920
Thank you for not letting go of my hand.

1144
01:06:24,280 --> 01:06:26,360
Thank you for letting me
stand here again,

1145
01:06:27,840 --> 01:06:29,120
alongside everyone.

1146
01:06:29,920 --> 01:06:30,880
Thank you.

1147
01:06:33,520 --> 01:06:36,200
Whoa, look at that move!

1148
01:06:37,160 --> 01:06:40,400
How could I let go
of my number one Support that easily?

1149
01:07:04,400 --> 01:07:07,800
♪The answer is you
whenever I ask my heart,♪

1150
01:07:07,840 --> 01:07:11,160
♪Can't get over you
though I try so hard♪

1151
01:07:11,280 --> 01:07:15,160
♪I'm afraid that
love could pull us apart♪

1152
01:07:15,200 --> 01:07:18,200
♪If I'm the only one
who's loving with all my heart♪

1153
01:07:18,360 --> 01:07:21,480
♪So many times I've rehearsed the line♪

1154
01:07:21,560 --> 01:07:25,000
♪To tell you that I wish you were mine,♪

1155
01:07:25,040 --> 01:07:31,880
♪But I turn into a coward every time
you look in my eyes♪

1156
01:07:32,080 --> 01:07:35,880
♪Maybe the risk is too high to take,♪

1157
01:07:35,960 --> 01:07:39,400
♪Just being near you
is enough for my sake,♪

1158
01:07:39,440 --> 01:07:46,200
♪But my heart beats so fast
that I can't fake♪

1159
01:07:46,240 --> 01:07:49,400
♪I'll find my way
into your heart one day,♪

1160
01:07:49,440 --> 01:07:52,040
♪Getting a little closer every day,♪

1161
01:07:52,040 --> 01:07:54,600
♪Before you even look my way,♪

1162
01:07:56,520 --> 01:07:59,440
♪Before you realize I'm here to stay♪

1163
01:07:59,960 --> 01:08:03,080
♪For now,
I'll just keep things brotherly♪

1164
01:08:03,080 --> 01:08:05,520
♪While caring for you secretly♪

1165
01:08:05,560 --> 01:08:08,560
♪I'll leave no signs for you to see♪

1166
01:08:09,760 --> 01:08:15,600
♪Until your heart makes room for me♪

